      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Doing a simple `rustc +1.98.1 --target wasm32-unknown-emscripten foo.rs` gives the following warning:\n```\nwarning: linker stderr: emcc: WASM_BIGINT is deprecated (no longer needed. Should only ever be implicitly disabled by -sWASM=0). Please open a bug if you have a continuing need for this setting [-Wdeprecated]\n  |\n  = note: `#[warn(linker_messages)]` on by default\n\nwarning: 1 warning emitted\n```\n\nI can see two options for resolving this:\n1. Remove `-sWASM_BIGINT` from the default linker arguments. This would be simplest, but might drop support for older emsdk versions though, I'm unsure whether this is a problem? Which versions of emsdk we support?\n2. Tweak the `linker_messages` lint to filter out this warning. This is a bit more involved, but it's done for loads of other messages, so it wouldn't be a big issue.\n\nCC target maintainers @hoodmane @juntyr, WDYT we should do here?",
